      "value": "@{6378a529aeb6384f691bd881|full_name}: yup, so if it's a lot of players that sounds like a pretty normal framerate, even maybe a bit above average.\nCheck with other people and see what they're getting. You may be surprised to hear them say they're struggling along at 20 or 30 fps.\nPerhaps if this performance is not good enough for you, you could talk to people about optimizing their avatars or the world. There's only so much VRChat can do when people have dozens of meshes and materials.\nAgain, cpu usage percentage has no correlation to performance. Being at 20% usage does not mean you should be able to get 4 times the framerate.",
